---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { START_URL } from "../lib/brand";

const description =
  "Vibe code with a CTO in the tools you already use. Move from rules and skills to an MCP when you want memory.";

const questions = ["Is my app production-ready?", "Is it secure?", "Will it support users?"];

const tools = [
  { name: "Claude", src: "/connectors/claude-color.svg" },
  { name: "ChatGPT", src: "/connectors/openai.svg" },
  { name: "Cursor", src: "/connectors/cursor.svg" },
  { name: "bolt.new", src: "/connectors/bolt.svg" },
  { name: "Base44", src: "/connectors/base44.png" },
  { name: "Lovable", src: "/connectors/lovable.svg" },
  { name: "v0", src: "/connectors/v0.svg" },
  { name: "Replit", src: "/connectors/replit.svg" },
];
---

<Base title="MCP — Stephan Smith" description={description}>
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
        Fractional CTO as a service
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-4xl dark:text-neutral-50">
        Ready to get the MCP?
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
        Most companies need a little technical leadership, not all of it. If you are vibe coding
        something, you can get it inside the tools you already build in, without booking hundreds of
        hours. Smart people build good apps when they have guidance and perspective — they do not need
        it done for them.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a
      href={START_URL}
      class="hero-cta mr-4 inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg px-7 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/35 sm:mr-8"
    >
      Upgrade to the MCP!
    </a>
  </section>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-2xl dark:text-neutral-50">
    Are you asking any of these questions?
  </h2>
  <ul class="mt-5 grid max-w-3xl gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
    {
      questions.map((question) => (
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-neutral-800 dark:bg-neutral-950">
          <p class="text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">{question}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-2xl dark:text-neutral-50">
    It fits the tool you already use
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
    Cursor, Claude, ChatGPT, and the other builders below — one of them, or all of them.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-5 flex list-none flex-wrap gap-3 p-0" aria-label="Tools the MCP fits">
    {
      tools.map((tool) => (
        <li>
          <span class="inline-flex h-12 items-center gap-3 rounded-full border border-neutral-200 bg-white pl-2.5 pr-5 text-base font-medium text-neutral-800 shadow-md shadow-neutral-900/10 dark:border-neutral-700 dark:bg-neutral-950 dark:text-neutral-100">
            <span class="flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white ring-1 ring-neutral-200 dark:ring-neutral-700">
              <img src={tool.src} alt="" width="20" height="20" class="h-5 w-5 object-contain" />
            </span>
            {tool.name}
          </span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-2xl dark:text-neutral-50">
    Okay, how does this work?
  </h2>
  <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-lg text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
    <p>
      You enable your account, then plug this into your AI tools. I do not code it for you. I do
      not tell your AI what to do. I help you understand where you stand — context and perspective
      on very specific parts of the app-building process.
    </p>
    <p>
      The right question at the right time unlocks the right answer. Once you are set up, we will
      give you a few prompts to help you get started.
    </p>
    <p>When you are actually stuck, I have more options. But lets wait until you are actually stuck!</p>
    <p>You got this!</p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-2xl dark:text-neutral-50">
    Why move from rules and skills
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
    Rules and skills take you part of the way. You move to an MCP when you want memory, so your
    prompts can pull in deeper context.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
    This comes with a subscription.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-8">
    <a
      href={START_URL}
      class="inline-flex rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 px-6 py-3.5 text-lg font-semibold text-white hover:bg-neutral-800 dark:bg-neutral-100 dark:text-neutral-900 dark:hover:bg-white"
    >
      Get the Full MCP
    </a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero-cta {
    background-image: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      #34d399 0%,
      #14b882 22%,
      #059669 48%,
      #047857 100%
    );
  }

  @keyframes hero-cta-pulse {
    0%,
    100% {
      transform: scale(1);
    }
    50% {
      transform: scale(1.045);
    }
  }

  .hero-cta:hover {
    animation: hero-cta-pulse 0.9s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .hero-cta:hover {
      animation: none;
    }
  }
</style>
